Google says:

Results ... about 39,800 for leprechaun (cobbler OR shoemaker)

So, figure out some spiffy new leather boots your
leprechauns might be crafting/carrying:

YANI "boots of mugging" might be a nice idea, to add
a capability often requested, thievery. They'd be
boots whose ultimate sneakiness gives some chance of
the PC sneaking up and lifting an object from the
grasp/inventory of a living, awake monster.

If the chance were low but useful, there'd be a
splendid trade-off problem between wearing those
boots and several other also useful ones.

xanthian.

But if leprechauns are nighttime shoemakers, how
could all the leprechauns in a leprechaun hall be
asleep? Surely if the PC walks barefoot around a
level with a sleeping leprechaun, a great racket of
cobbling to make shoes/boots for the PC will
suddenly arise, awakening all monsters on the level?

YANIs are best when they involve trade-offs.



